Lab: Multi-step process with no access control on one step

Goal:-     This lab has an admin panel with a flawed multi-step process for changing a user's role. You can familiarize yourself with the admin panel by logging in using the credentials administrator:admin.
To solve the lab, log in using the credentials wiener:peter and exploit the flawed access controls to promote yourself to become an administrator. 

Observation:- #The role-change functionality follows a multi step workflow.
              #The first step requires admin privileges and initiates the role change.
              #The second step is a confirmation request that finalizes the action.
              #Proper access control is enforced in the initial step but missing in the confirmation step.
              #By replaying the confirmation request with a normal user session, privilege escalation becomes possible.

Steps to solve :- 
        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Login using administrator credential 
        Step3:- Change role of carlos from normal to administrator and capture the request in the burpsuit 
        Step4:- Now confirm for the request and capture the request in burpsuit
        step5:- now loging as given credential of normal user
        Step6:- go to my account and capture the reqest in burpsuit 
        Step6:- chnage the request type of request of carlos from post to get of confirmation request
        Step7:- Change cookie session (replace carlos cookiee with wiener) change name from carlos to wiener of confirmation request
        Step8:- Send reqest 

Root Cause:- #Access control validation was applied only to the initial step of the workflow.
             #The confirmation endpoint trusted previously initiated actions without re verifying user authorization.
             #Lack of authorization checks on every step of the multi step process allowed unauthorized users to complete privileged actions.

Vulnerability Type:- Broken Access Control

                     Multi-Step Process Access Control Bypass

